        "date": "2026-11-10T01:16:40Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(machines): Tormach 8L and 15L Slant-PRO lathe definitions\n\nTwo shipped lathe machines from Tormach's public spec sheets, so\nturning programs are judged against a real Tormach lathe envelope and\ncan be checked in PathPilot Hub's 8L / 15L:\n\n- 8L: X 4.5 in, Z 10 in, 180-2500 / 350-5000 rpm (two ranges, 5C),\n  150 IPM, 99-entry tool table (gang / QCTP).\n- 15L Slant-PRO: X 10 in, Z 12 in, 180-2500 rpm (6 in chuck), 60 IPM,\n  8-station turret.\n\nInch, full-stroke-either-way travel like the shipped Tormach mills.\nThe 8L's 4.5 in X and the 15L's chuck-rated 2500 rpm are the\nconservative readings; sources and choices in the decision record.\nPinned by tormach_lathes (2 tests).\n\nFixes #611\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
